            "command": [
              "bash",
              "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh",
              "<mutated check_model_parity.sh>"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "aa27c50cf30294c9807b70c19836871bf94f85a27c6a5bd33d5c2426a06b58c0",
            "failure_scenario": "A later edit drops choom or the reason and the guard stays green.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "t1-dirs-passes-a-commented-export",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "dirs() reads the first line matching export CARGO_TARGET_DIR= inside t1_deep and t1_dogfood, with no check that the line is code. A commented-out export passes it: dirs returns 0 on an autopilot whose t1_deep export is commented, and deep then builds into the shared target dir the guard exists to prevent. The shared-deep mutant deletes the line and is killed; a comment is not. Fix: skip lines whose first non-space character is #."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 128
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "cm_dirs.sh",
              "<autopilot with deep export commented>"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "54f945b0240728dc6b84b8866874a871b8d6fbc67affbdb843a75cff58920704",
            "failure_scenario": "A developer comments the export while debugging; the guard stays green and deep and dogfood race on one target dir.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "antigravity",
          "version": "1.3.0"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": []
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-guard_blind_spots_comments",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The `locked` guard uses a grep pipeline that does not filter out comments, allowing a commented-out `flock` command to satisfy the check and create a vacuous pass."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 121
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark asserted. locked() greps the line before the parity call without dropping comments, so a commented flock line would satisfy it. Same class as t1-dirs-passes-a-commented-export; read, not run: agreed.",
            "failure_scenario": "If a developer comments out the `flock` lock wrapper around the `parity` measurement, the `grep -B1 ... | grep -c 'flock'` check will still find the commented-out `flock` string and pass the check. This causes a vacuous pass while the actual lock is not taken, bypassing the intended guard.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-timing_guard_seconds_granularity",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The timing guard in t-red depends on the 1-second granularity of $SECONDS, creating a race condition where C_SECS can be evaluated as 2 instead of 3."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 76
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark asserted. Contradicted: the red case sleeps at least 3 s, and floor(s+e)-floor(s) >= floor(e), so a whole-second difference cannot read below 3; the upper bounds have 2+ s margin.",
            "failure_scenario": "If t0 is captured immediately before the second ticks (e.g., at 0.999s), and the 3-second sleep in the models lane finishes slightly under 3 seconds (e.g., at 3.900s real time), the SECONDS variable will have advanced by only 2 ticks (from X to X+2). C_SECS will evaluate to 2, causing the `[ \"$C_SECS\" -ge 3 ]` guard to fail spuriously.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-orphaned_processes_mutant_test",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The test harness leaves orphaned process groups when the `no-trap` mutant is tested, as `case_run` only sends `TERM` to the harness shell."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 72
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark asserted. Contradicted: the stub children only sleep for the case duration and child_gone checks deep; no lasting orphan.",
            "failure_scenario": "During the `no-trap` mutant test, `case_run` sends `TERM` to the `harness.sh` process. Because the mutant removes the trap, `harness.sh` terminates immediately without propagating the signal to the process groups of `deep`, `dogfood`, and `models`. These processes continue running in the background as orphans for up to 20 seconds.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-inverted_exits_term_trap",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The `autopilot.sh` trap converts `INT`/`TERM` signals into an exit code of `1` (via `die`), which is an inverted exit behavior compared to the `143` it demands from its child lanes."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/autopilot.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 189
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark asserted. Contradicted: die exits 1 on an interrupt by design; the guard requires non-zero, and the no-trap mutant is what gives 143.",
            "failure_scenario": "If the CI environment or an operator sends a `TERM` signal to `autopilot.sh` to gracefully abort it, the script's trap catches it and calls `die`, which runs `exit 1`. This exits the script with a generic error code (1) rather than the standard termination code (143), masking the signal termination from the caller.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
